I personally would like to be able to place lots of different inventory
windows all over the place, where clicking the mouse an object does what 
you normally do with that object, e.g., all armor, rings, amulets and 
blindfolds go into a window where clicking on an item either puts it
on or takes it off (replacing P,T,W,R).  Clicking on an item in a tool
window would apply that tool, popping up a dialog or selection box if
necessary.  Also, in shops you could have a window of unpaid items, and
click on the ones you want to pay for.  When reading a scroll of identify
up pops a window of what you have so that you mouse on the ones to 
identify. 

In fact, the way xrn looks is a pretty good layout, with an upper window
for the usual game messages, and information bar with a bunch of buttons
below it, a big text window where the dungeon could go, and each of it's
dialog and composition subwindows have info bars, scroll bars and few
buttons to push.  Maybe the basic framework could be 'liberated' from
an existing app?


